# .spool/reporter/reporter.req

feature: REPORTER

requirements:

  - id: REPORTER-1
    title: Report Generation
    description: >
      The reporter must generate a Report struct from the
      index that captures the full traceability summary
      across all features.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Separating report data from report presentation means
      all formatters work from the same data structure and
      formatting concerns are fully isolated from data
      collection concerns.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-1-1
        title: Accurate Totals
        description: >
          Given a populated index,
          when a report is generated,
          then the Report struct contains accurate totals for
          requirements, ACs, linked ACs, untested ACs, and
          orphaned annotations across all features.

      - id: REPORTER-1-2
        title: Per-Feature Totals
        description: >
          Given a populated index,
          when a report is generated,
          then the Report struct contains a FeatureReport
          for each feature in the index with accurate
          per-feature totals reflecting only active requirements,
          and a separate count of excluded superseded and
          deprecated requirements.

      - id: REPORTER-1-3
        title: Untested ACs List
        description: >
          Given a populated index,
          when a report is generated,
          then the Report struct contains the full list of
          untested ACs with their IDs and descriptions.

      - id: REPORTER-1-4
        title: Orphaned Annotations List
        description: >
          Given a populated index,
          when a report is generated,
          then the Report struct contains the full list of
          orphaned annotations with their file paths and
          line numbers.

      - id: REPORTER-1-5
        title: Empty Report
        description: >
          Given an empty index,
          when a report is generated,
          then a valid Report struct with zero totals is
          returned and no error is produced.

  - id: REPORTER-2
    title: Formatter Interface
    description: >
      The reporter must expose a Formatter interface that
      allows multiple output formats to be supported and
      third party formatters to be registered.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      A published Formatter interface keeps output format
      concerns fully decoupled from report data concerns,
      allows the compiled-in formatter set to be extended
      without modifying core code, and enables community
      formatters for formats Spool does not ship with.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-2-1
        title: Minimal Interface Contract
        description: >
          Given the published Formatter interface,
          then it must expose only Format(report *Report)
          ([]byte, error) as a required method.

      - id: REPORTER-2-2
        title: Third-Party Formatter
        description: >
          Given a third party formatter that implements
          the Formatter interface,
          when it is passed to the reporter,
          then it produces output from the same Report
          struct as compiled-in formatters.

  - id: REPORTER-3
    title: Plain Text Formatter
    description: >
      Spool must ship a plain text formatter producing
      a human readable report suitable for terminal output.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Plain text is the universal fallback for developer
      tooling output. It requires no rendering, works in
      any terminal, and is immediately readable without
      additional tooling.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-3-1
        title: Summary Table
        description: >
          Given a populated Report struct,
          when the plain text formatter is applied,
          then the output contains a summary table with
          per-feature rows showing req, AC, linked,
          untested, and orphaned counts.

      - id: REPORTER-3-2
        title: Untested ACs Listed
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing untested ACs,
          when the plain text formatter is applied,
          then each untested AC is listed with its ID
          and description.

      - id: REPORTER-3-3
        title: Orphaned Listed
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing orphaned annotations,
          when the plain text formatter is applied,
          then each orphaned annotation is listed with its
          file path, line number, and referenced ID.

      - id: REPORTER-3-4
        title: No Issues Message
        description: >
          Given a Report struct with no untested ACs and
          no orphaned annotations,
          when the plain text formatter is applied,
          then the output indicates full traceability
          with no issues found.

      - id: REPORTER-3-5
        title: Excluded Reqs Shown
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing superseded or
          deprecated requirements,
          when the plain text formatter is applied,
          then the per-feature summary indicates the count
          of excluded requirements alongside the active totals.

  - id: REPORTER-4
    title: JSON Formatter
    description: >
      Spool must ship a JSON formatter producing machine
      readable output suitable for CI tooling and piping.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      JSON output allows CI pipelines, scripts, and third
      party tools to consume Spool report data without
      screen scraping plain text. It also provides a stable
      contract for tooling built on top of Spool reports.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-4-1
        title: Valid JSON Output
        description: >
          Given a populated Report struct,
          when the JSON formatter is applied,
          then the output is valid JSON containing all
          report data including totals, per-feature
          breakdowns, untested ACs, and orphaned annotations.

      - id: REPORTER-4-2
        title: CamelCase Field Names
        description: >
          Given a populated Report struct,
          when the JSON formatter is applied,
          then the JSON structure mirrors the Report struct
          hierarchy with camelCase field names.

  - id: REPORTER-5
    title: Markdown Formatter
    description: >
      Spool must ship a markdown formatter producing output
      suitable for inclusion in pull request comments,
      wiki pages, and project documentation.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Markdown output allows Spool reports to be dropped
      directly into GitLab or GitHub PR comments, wiki pages,
      or README files without any transformation. This is
      particularly valuable for teams that want to include
      traceability status in their PR review process.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-5-1
        title: Markdown Table
        description: >
          Given a populated Report struct,
          when the markdown formatter is applied,
          then the output contains a valid markdown table
          with per-feature rows showing req, AC, linked,
          untested, and orphaned counts.

      - id: REPORTER-5-2
        title: Untested Section
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing untested ACs,
          when the markdown formatter is applied,
          then each untested AC is listed under a dedicated
          markdown section with its ID and description.

      - id: REPORTER-5-3
        title: Orphaned Section
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing orphaned annotations,
          when the markdown formatter is applied,
          then each orphaned annotation is listed under a
          dedicated markdown section with its file path,
          line number, and referenced ID.

      - id: REPORTER-5-4
        title: Excluded Reqs in Table
        description: >
          Given a Report struct containing superseded or
          deprecated requirements,
          when the markdown formatter is applied,
          then the per-feature table indicates the count of
          excluded requirements alongside the active totals.

  - id: REPORTER-6
    title: Report Output
    description: >
      The reporter must write formatted output to the
      configured destination.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Project Lead
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-03-23
    rationale: >
      Separating output destination from formatting means
      the same formatter can write to stdout during local
      development and to a file in CI without any change
      to the formatter itself.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: REPORTER-6-1
        title: Write to Stdout
        description: >
          Given an output destination of stdout,
          when the report is written,
          then formatted output is written to stdout.

      - id: REPORTER-6-2
        title: Write to File
        description: >
          Given an output destination of a file path,
          when the report is written,
          then formatted output is written to that file,
          creating it if it does not exist.

      - id: REPORTER-6-3
        title: Unwritable Destination Error
        description: >
          Given an output destination of a file path
          that cannot be written to,
          when the report is written,
          then a descriptive error is returned.